      "status": "candidate_hardening_deviation",
      "mapping_note": "Intentional lifetime hardening. Module exit unregisters the platform driver before destroying shared client storage, so the registered per-device .remove callback runs for bound output consumers and clears/puts their SMEM state handles under rdbg_smem_state_lock. A final guarded sweep releases any remaining module-owned handles, and cleanup releases the full character-device range reserved at init. Runtime unbind/rebind, active input IRQs, and open-file behavior remain unverified.",
